Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:51:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/71] Send the reasoning effort instead of inheriting GLM's
 max default
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The chat adapter turned thinking on but never forwarded a depth, and GLM
reads a missing `reasoning_effort` as `max` — the deepest and most expensive
rung it offers. Every request was running there, and whatever the user chose
in the model picker was dropped on the way to the wire.

The ladder GLM-5.3 accepts is only `low`, `high` and `max`; any other value
is rejected outright, so an effort inherited from a config written for
another provider has to be projected onto one of the three rather than
forwarded. Clamping at the wire boundary keeps the rest of Codex on its own
wider ladder. Rungs with no depth ordering to project fall back to `high`,
which is the model default.

`thinking` stays pinned to enabled: GLM-5.3 errors on `disabled`, so depth
is the only dial left.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 codex-rs/codex-api/src/requests/chat.rs | 62 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 61 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

